anarchy@a state of lawlessness and disorder@1
archive@a depository containing historical records and documents@001
civilization@a society in an advanced state of social development@001
clergy@the entire class of religious officials in Christianity@01
constitution@the act of forming or establishing something@01
curator@the custodian of a collection, as a museum or library@1
demographic@a statistic characterizing human populations@1
diplomacy@negotiation between nations@1
domestic@of or relating to the home@001
dynasty@a sequence of powerful leaders in the same family@01
empire@the domain ruled by a single authoritative sovereign@001
enlightenment@education that results in the spread of knowledge@01
impeach@bring an accusation against@001
monotheistic@believing that there is only one god@01
monarchy@autocracy governed by a ruler who usually inherits authority@1
patriarch@the male head of family or tribe@01
segregation@the act of keeping apart@1
suffrage@the right to vote in political discussions@001
theocracy@government ruled by religious leaders@01
totalitarianism@government in which the ruler is an absolute dictator@01
tyranny@a form of government in which the ruler is unconstrained@01
